Falsifies `file_allocation_table::directory::verification::a_directory_reads_only_its_own_sectors`.

The defect: a chain directory takes one sector more from each cluster than the cluster holds, so
it reads the first sector of the next cluster on the volume, which belongs to some other file, or
the sector past the data region.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(sector >= first_data && sector < first_data + data_sectors)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@
                     };
                     // The walk yields only data clusters, which always have sectors.
                     *next = boot.cluster_first_sector(cluster)?;
-                    *remaining = boot.sectors_per_cluster();
+                    *remaining = boot.sectors_per_cluster() + 1;
                 }
                 *remaining -= 1;
                 *next += 1;
